## Conventions

All variables are real. Every square root is the principal nonnegative root;
in particular, $\sqrt{u^2}=|u|$, not automatically $u$. Simplification preserves
the original domain and every nonzero-denominator restriction. Stipulated
strict positivity is retained even when a resulting formula extends further.
The Latin labels below correspond by ordinal to the original labels:
a = U+0430, b = U+0431, c = U+0432, d = U+0433, e = U+0434,
